[
    {
        "content": "<p><code>PiTensorProduct</code> provides powerful API for working with families of vector spaces with many useful results such as <code>projectiveSeminorm</code>, however I have found it notoriously difficult to work with when only few vector spaces are involved. For example transforming something as simple as</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">X</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⊗</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Y</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>into a respective <code>PiTensorProduct</code> took me considerable effort:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">LinearAlgebra</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">PiTensorProduct</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Basic</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">LinearAlgebra</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">TensorProduct</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Map</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Algebra</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Module</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">ULift</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">open</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">PiTensorProduct</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">TensorProduct</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">universe</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">u</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">w</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">variable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">CommSemiring</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">variable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">E</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">u</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">AddCommMonoid</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">E</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Module</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">E</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">variable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">F</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">AddCommMonoid</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">F</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Module</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">F</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">variable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Unit</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⊕</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Unit</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">instance</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Unit</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⊕</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Unit</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">AddCommMonoid</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Sum</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">elim</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">↦</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ULift</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">v</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">E</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">↦</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ULift</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">u</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">F</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">inl</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ULift</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">addCommMonoid</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">inr</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ULift</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">addCommMonoid</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">instance</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Unit</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⊕</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Unit</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Module</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Sum</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">elim</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">↦</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ULift</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">v</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">E</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">↦</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ULift</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">u</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">F</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">inl</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ULift</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">module'</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">inr</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ULift</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">module'</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">abbrev</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">binaryPiTensorProduct</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">⨂</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Unit</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⊕</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Unit</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Sum</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">elim</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">↦</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ULift</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">v</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">E</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">↦</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ULift</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">u</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">F</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">check</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">binaryPiTensorProduct</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">E</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">F</span>\n\n<span class=\"sd\">/-- Linear equivalence between the family tensor product over `Unit ⊕ Unit`</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">and the binary tensor product of the two component spaces, even when they</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">live in different universes. -/</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">noncomputable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">binaryEquivPiTensor</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">binaryPiTensorProduct</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">E</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">F</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≃ₗ</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">E</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⊗</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">F</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">((</span><span class=\"n\">tmulEquivDep</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Sum</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">elim</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">↦</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ULift</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">v</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">E</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">↦</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ULift</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">u</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">F</span><span class=\"o\">)))</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">symm</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">trans</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">TensorProduct</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">congr</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">subsingletonEquiv</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Unit</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">unit</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">subsingletonEquiv</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Unit</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">unit</span><span class=\"o\">)))</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">trans</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">TensorProduct</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">congr</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ULift</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">moduleEquiv</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ULift</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">moduleEquiv</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">check</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">binaryEquivPiTensor</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">E</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">F</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>main hurdles are:</p>\n<ol>\n<li>possibility of different universe levels of constituent spaces E, F</li>\n<li>need for proving dependent instances for AddCommMonoid and Module for each indexed family</li>\n<li>quite involved syntax for introducing and handling sum types</li>\n</ol>\n<p>These are of course not uncircumventable, as shown in the example above, but in general I think that such a simple pattern should have a simple solution. Do you think it would be worth including a collection of such <code>def</code>s in mathlib? If yes, what would be the most suitable place for it?</p>",
        "id": 608538211,
        "sender_full_name": "Michał Pacholski",
        "timestamp": 1783370168
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>For 1, I think Mathlib's monoidal structure in Representation.Rep is relevant. Usually, the category of k-representations for a monoid G, denoted by<code>Rep k G</code>, has three universe arguments: <code>(k : Type u) (G : Type v) (V : Type w)</code> and we write <code>Rep.{w} k G</code> to explicitly fix a universe w for the underlying modules. However, as soon as you wish to provide a monoidal structure instance, you have to provide a tensor <code>unit</code>. In Mathlib, this is given by <code>Rep.of trivial k G k</code>. Here the underlying module <code>k</code> of the trivial representation we provide lives in the universe 'u', not 'w', because we fixed <code>(k : Type u)</code> at the begining. Therefore, whenever you need to use this particular monoidal structure, you will see <code>Rep.{u} k G</code> in Mathlib. Otherwise, Lean complains the universe dismatch issue, which indeed is pretty annoying.</p>",
        "id": 608876398,
        "sender_full_name": "Jiaxi Mo",
        "timestamp": 1783482105
    }
]